Make HLL deserialization reject inconsistent images.

Found by data.sketches tools/fuzz under ASan and UBSan, all on hll_sketch
deserialization:

- AuxHashMap::deserialize: lgAuxArrInts from the image was a shift count
  (UB above 31); it is now bounded by lg_k. The pairs are read with memcpy
  rather than through a uint32_t pointer at an arbitrary offset (misaligned
  load). The map is owned by a unique_ptr until returned, so a duplicate slot
  no longer leaks it; in the stream overload it was freed explicitly and
  then again by its unique_ptr (double free).
- CouponHashSet::newSet: lgArrInts likewise bounded by lg_k (shift UB), and
  an updatable image's count must equal its non-empty slots: otherwise a
  later compact serialization writes every slot into a buffer sized for the
  count (heap-buffer-overflow WRITE).
- HllArray::newHll: aux entries in a non-HLL_4 image are rejected (the cast
  to Hll4Array was invalid: UBSan downcast), and an HLL_4 image must have an
  aux entry, of at least curMin + 15, for exactly the slots that carry
  AUX_TOKEN; queries, printing and serialization otherwise throw on, or
  read, entries that are not there.
- CouponList and CouponHashSet: every coupon must be a real coupon (non-zero
  value field) and appear once, and an updatable set's table is rebuilt by
  inserting its coupons instead of copied: the image is not trusted to place
  them where the hash probe finds them, and a misplaced coupon was rewritten
  on the next round trip. A set too large to stay a set is corruption, and
  the promoted sketch is freed rather than leaked.
- CouponList: an image flagged empty must count no coupons (it is not read,
  and a non-zero count made a sketch of that many zero coupons).

